@@name
research
@@description
Answer the question in the user request by reading the code and sources; this is investigation only.
@@requirements
    - Cite file paths and line numbers (or URLs) for every claim
    - Separate verified facts from inferences, and label inferences
    - End with a direct answer or recommendation
@@approach
    Before reading widely, reason through:
    - Which files, docs or data most directly answer the question
    - What evidence would change the answer
    Read those sources first, then widen only as needed.
@@verification
    - Spot-check each cited path or line exists and says what the report claims
@@constraints
    - Read-only: make no edits to files in the working directory
    - Do not run commands that modify state (installs, migrations, deploys)
@@out-of-scope
    - Implementing any fix or change the research suggests
